From: lunatickochiya <125438787@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ovpn-dco: define OVPN_NO_WQ_PERCPU for Linux 6.6

ovpn-backports 7.3.0 uses WQ_PERCPU, which only exists in Linux 6.7+.
The upstream Makefile detects it in the top-level Makefile, but
OpenWrt builds only drivers/net/ovpn with M=..., so that ccflags-y is
never applied and the module fails with:

  drivers/net/ovpn/main.c:325:43: error: 'WQ_PERCPU' undeclared

Pass OVPN_NO_WQ_PERCPU through NOSTDINC_FLAGS; the package's
compat-include/linux/workqueue.h then defines WQ_PERCPU as 0, which is
the pre-6.7 behavior (CPU-bound workqueues are the default).

---
diff --git a/kernel/ovpn-dco/Makefile b/kernel/ovpn-dco/Makefile
index 8fb1b6d..9b5d3b7 100644
--- a/kernel/ovpn-dco/Makefile
+++ b/kernel/ovpn-dco/Makefile
@@ -48,6 +48,8 @@ NOSTDINC_FLAGS += \
 	-I$(PKG_BUILD_DIR)/compat-include \
 	-include $(PKG_BUILD_DIR)/linux-compat.h
 
+NOSTDINC_FLAGS += -DOVPN_NO_WQ_PERCPU
+
 EXTRA_KCONFIG:= \
 	CONFIG_OVPN=m
 
